{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/879765-sell-me-on-hunter-the-vigil","id":879765,"title":"Sell me on Hunter: The Vigil.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-01T16:52:42-07:00","id":879765,"title":"Sell me on Hunter: The Vigil.","content":"I gained a Hunter the vigil rulebook from a friend, and I've never had any interest in Hunter before so I would like to know the appeal in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:01:30-07:00","id":879773,"title":"","content":"It's a game about normal people dealing with the unnatural and the terrible cost of that. It's about not having any of the answers and trying to figure out what the hell is going on. While the monsters of the Chronicles of Darkness world are mostly free to rampage and screw with mortals all they like, you're the brave, stupid few who try and fight back. Whether you're alone and holding a cheap rifle from Wal-Mart or an initiated member of an occult conspiracy that stretches back thousands of years, you don't really know what the big picture looks like and the odds are severely stacked against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:41:16-07:00","id":879800,"title":"","content":"I don't understand why Firefox keeps crashing when I'm halfway into writing a post on this forum. It seems to happen more frequently than any other site I visit.<br /> <br /> Vigil has two strengths. One: it strikes an excellent balance between versatility and customizability, and having definition to inspire ideas.<br /> <br /> Do you want to be four guys operating out of Steve's garage, planning out your opening to jump and sackbeat the sleazy guy one of you saw drinking a woman's blood one foggy night? That's in the corebook.<br /> Do you want to be the same four guys, but your buddies at work and your friends at the bowling alley lend you a sympathetic ear because they've seen some weird shit themselves and never had the boldness to speak up, so now they can keep an eye on the creepy blood guy for you when you're not looking, and slip you a pass through the employees only door when you need the evidence to prove your suspicions? That's in the corebook.<br /> Do you want to be the chosen few, burdened with a terrible destiny and fighting a perilous but successful battle to keep yourself on the side of the angels while you turn the literal fires of Hell upon the demons whose blood you share? That's in the corebook, including the literal Hellfire.<br /> Ghost hunters using Kirlian cameras and EVP analysis to uncover the science behind real hauntings? Corebook.<br /> Paramilitary special operations team armed with classified weapons technology to bust werewolves on the President's dime? Corebook.<br /> Grassroots congregations of the faithful who gather after prayer meetings to seek out monsters and save their souls for the Lord, or failing that, to cast them back to the Pit from whence they came? Corebook.<br /> Culture jammers hunting video footage of Bigfoot to grow their Youtube channel subscription base? Corebook.<br /> It scales up, it scales down.<br /> <br /> Two: Hunter books are a strong distillation of the Chronicles of Darkness at their best, in presenting a world filled with dangerous Fortean anomalies that can't all be easily categorized. They're not just about dudes banding together to exterminate the other big monster gamelines, although if you want to do that, it is absolutely something Hunter does without complaint. But you've also got alien architecture in the rifts between cities, totemic prophecies lurking behind the birth of the United States, living bronze ants from the time of the pharaohs who consume the human brain from within and operate the body like a puppet, and lurching men who survive impossible injuries not out of any sorcery or spiritual heritage, but simply out of their sheer, overwhelming urge to kill.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hunters live in a strange world, and they've often only got each other and a handful of lead to make sense of it. That's all right. Sometimes, that's enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T18:03:01-07:00","id":879810,"title":"","content":"In a completely opposite direction from the previous posts, Hunter also makes a great tool for other games. They make for fantastic unexpected opponents in nearly any story, and scale very well with whatever scope your game is. Are your Vampires freshly Embraced and prone to making mistakes? You get idiots with videocameras trying to post them on Youtube and the angry friends of their last meal trying to put them down. Are your Vampires pushing a couple centuries of unlife? You get SWAT teams with vampire-detecting goggles and vengeful blood sorcerers coming for them the second they step out of line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T07:13:07-07:00","id":880142,"title":"","content":"As mentioned previously, Hunter's core appeal is in its versatility. It isn't really one game so much as its a dozen games with enough shared elements that they can comfortably cohabitate in a single book. Miraculously.<br /> <br /> Do you want to use it as a patch or an expansion to build off an existing mortals game? Easily accomplished. You can focus on investigation and discovery with Hunter as easily as killing monsters. Even in the killing monsters department it has a huge range. Do you want a claustrophobic, paranoid game about fighting an unseen adversary alone with only a baseball bat and a kitchen knife? Done. Do you want to lead a team of highly trained combat warlocks in a guns blazing raid to exterminate a nest of unholy abominations? Also done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:27:14-07:00","id":880271,"title":"","content":"I really liked all the answers. I've read some of the rulebook and I'm liking it. I thought it would be just a game of just kill monsters with no real deep to it but I was wrong. It does look interesting at minimum and really fun at beast, which is good. I'll talk to my group and see if they are up to play it. I strongly believe that we are going to have fun. Thank you all for the answers, I hope this post helps other people that want to know about Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:45:29-07:00","id":880429,"title":"","content":"I enjoy hunter because by wielding the power 'necessary' to defeat the monsters of the world you dance the line of monster and mortal yourself. Then you have the risk of learning a truth that could undermine your entire drive and new found purpose. What if not all monsters are evil? <br /> <br /> Hunter can be just a monster of the week, bust down the door and kill everything that isn't a mundane human but it can also be so much more.<br /> <br /> For instance I have a character who is a lucifuge demonologist that uses 'evil' and the powers such can grant to have the strength to stand toe to toe with monsters. The ends justify the means type of character who willingly forsakes himself to save others. So not only does he have to hide his methods from other hunters and from the lucifuge themselves because of being a radical even among them but there is the possibility that one good monster could make him doubt very self imposed purpose.<br /> <br /> So hunter unlike other lines allows you to willingly make yourself into a monster without noticing how far each little choice will take you until you are like the monsters you hunt. The big difference is they were made into what they are almost entirely against their will yet you chose to be their equal. These monsters in the dark must live in shadow in order to survive but you had a chance to live in a world of light. Yes you hunt because you saw into the darkness but why did you stand tall when others cower? Are you so different from the monsters you label as evil? Especially now as you slay beings just trying to survive are you so different? They were the stories told to scare you as a child and you have become the horror that monsters warn their children of. You are a hunter the lone thing that monsters fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:57:50-07:00","id":883867,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Vigil is has one thing that the other splats do not have: Indiana Jones! Seriously, they got a Greek version of Indiana Jones called the Aegis Kai Doru that hunts, preserves, and uses magical Relics that can do some cool stuff like one-eyed pennies that let you eavesdrop on people and a spear talisman that works like an actual spear! They even got talking oracle heads and junk. That conspiracy and Cheiron Corp is what sold me on this splat. You'll love it too,Tangled Virus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:02:06-07:00","id":883868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/879765-sell-me-on-hunter-the-vigil?p=883867#post883867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter: the Vigil is has one thing that the other splats do not have: Indiana Jones! Seriously, they got a Greek version of Indiana Jones called the Aegis Kai Doru that hunts, preserves, and uses magical Relics that can do some cool stuff like one-eyed pennies that let you eavesdrop on people and a spear talisman that works like an actual spear! They even got talking oracle heads and junk. That conspiracy and Cheiron Corp is what sold me on this splat. You'll love it too,Tangled Virus.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do think the Aegis Kai Doru is cool and this is a cool reason to play Hunter, it's worth mentioning that this is also a hat the Mysterium wears in <i>Mage: The Awakening</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:16:27-07:00","id":883877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/879765-sell-me-on-hunter-the-vigil?p=883868#post883868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I do think the Aegis Kai Doru is cool and this is a cool reason to play Hunter, it's worth mentioning that this is also a hat the Mysterium wears in <i>Mage: The Awakening</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really? I had no idea. But what you have told me, this could be a good story hook as the Aegis races the witches for some mighty relic of Atlantis or something, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:36:20-07:00","id":883889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/879765-sell-me-on-hunter-the-vigil?p=883877#post883877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh really? I had no idea. But what you have told me, this could be a good story hook as the Aegis races the witches for some mighty relic of Atlantis or something, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. If anything, they're the two forces most likely to be hunting them, with Seers and other baddies following up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:42:20-07:00","id":883891,"title":"","content":"A major draw of Hunter, to me, is that I love an underdog story. The Chronicles of Darkness generally put mortal humans in the role of a background - they're victims and bystanders, maybe pawns. It's not as bad as it was in the old WoD, but still there. Hunter flips it over, and shows humanity biting back. Some of those weak, bog-standard mortals decide that they're not going to sit down and take it. And some magicians, blood-suckers or other aloof supernaturals are in for a nasty surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:58:09-07:00","id":886968,"title":"","content":"Does Hunter have a 2nd edition or is one planned or are they just sticking with 1st edition for now? If they are sticking with 1st edition, does it convert well to the new CofD changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T22:42:44-07:00","id":886994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/879765-sell-me-on-hunter-the-vigil?p=886968#post886968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Hunter have a 2nd edition or is one planned or are they just sticking with 1st edition for now? If they are sticking with 1st edition, does it convert well to the new CofD changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a second edition in the works; for the nonce, Mortal Remains serves as a CofD rules patch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:09:12-07:00","id":887138,"title":"","content":"I think they're planning to do a second edition of <i>everything </i>eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:52:16-07:00","id":896391,"title":"","content":"Dread powers. I like it you are able to make all sorts of monsters or opponents with one ruleset. To me it is the necessary supplement to the wod core rulebook. With these two books combined you can do a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}